:0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3728492173","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114413#issuecomment-3728492173","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114413","id":3728492173,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ePEaN","user":{"login":"JoNax97","id":10124534,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTI0NTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10124534?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97","html_url":"https://github.com/JoNax97","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-09T11:18:14Z","updated_at":"2026-01-09T11:18:14Z","body":"> Hey @JoNax97 - Do you mean something along the lines of `PROPERTY_HINT_CURVE` and/or `@export_curve` in gdscript. So the end user would do something like - `@export_curve(\"X Axis\", \"Y Axis\") var curve_res : Curve`\r\n> \r\nYes exactly! ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3728492173/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3745930192","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114413#issuecomment-3745930192","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114413","id":3745930192,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7fRlvQ","user":{"login":"kushagra10025","id":53115703,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTE1NzAz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53115703?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kushagra10025","html_url":"https://github.com/kushagra10025","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kushagra10025/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kushagra10025/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kushagra10025/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kushagra10025/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kushagra10025/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kushagra10025/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kushagra10025/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kushagra10025/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kushagra10025/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-13T19:03:33Z","updated_at":"2026-01-13T19:03:33Z","body":"Alright! I've updated the approach in this PR. Adding `PROPERTY_HINT_CURVE` did not make sense as Resources were being handled with `PROPERTY_HINT_RESOURCE_TYPE` - but I found they use `p_hint_string` to pass the Classes.\r\n\r\n**Approach**\r\nEdited `EditorPropertyResource` to allow parsing of additional `hint_strings` in addition to Class types. Tried to maintain existing func as is. The parser hooks and extracts the `hint_strings`. Then these are set as metadata `_custom_resource_hint_string`.\r\n\r\nIntention was - Pass the hint string and let the target editor handle the parsing and using as required.\r\n\r\nThe `syntax` post this would look something like this:\r\n* in gdscript\r\n```gdscript\r\n@export_custom(PROPERTY_HINT_RESOURCE_TYPE, \"Curve[Time(s);Velocity (m/s)]\") var acceleration_curve : Resource\r\n@export_custom(PROPERTY_HINT_RESOURCE_TYPE, \"Curve[Some X value (in newton);Y value (in m/s^2)]\") var other_curve : Curve\r\n```\r\n\r\n* in cpp - For dev purposes (not commited) edited the `cpu_particles_3d.cpp` as it exposes curves.\r\n```cpp\r\nADD_PROPERTYI(PropertyInfo(Variant::OBJECT, \"angular_velocity_curve\", PROPERTY_HINT_RESOURCE_TYPE, \"Curve[x_label;y_label]\"), \"set_param_curve\", \"get_param_curve\", PARAM_ANGULAR_VELOCITY);\r\n```\r\n\r\n* in c# - should be similar 😅\r\n\r\n**End Result**\r\n<img width=\"571\" height=\"416\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fbf57268-37ad-4ddc-bd7b-67e261c8963f\" />\r\n\r\nAnything which causes an update to property should, refresh the changes in the labels in the Curve editor. I'm a bit unsure about the refresh `hint_string update` section in `EditorPropertyResource::update_property` - any insights on this would be appreciated.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3745930192/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]